+    --cursor-drag-button=...
+        With --virtual-cursor-relative=, a second button that drags with the
+        cursor: hold it and move the cursor to drag from where it was pressed,
+        for example to draw a selection box. If --cursor-drag-tap= is given,
+        that point is tapped first. Released without moving, the button does
